  "notes": "{色|いろ}あせる means to fade or lose color, used both literally (fabric, photos) and figuratively (memories, value).\n\nWRITING:\nAlso written as {色褪|いろあ}せる.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{色|いろ}あせている describes a state of having already faded.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {色|いろ}あせた{写真|しゃしん}: faded photograph\n- {色|いろ}あせた{記憶|きおく}: faded memory\n- {色|いろ}あせない{魅力|みりょく}: timeless charm\n- {色|いろ}あせない{名曲|めいきょく}: a classic that doesn't lose its luster\n\nKEY USAGE:\nThe form {色|いろ}あせた (past) is very common as a prenominal modifier, and {色|いろ}あせない (negative) is often used to praise something timeless.",
